A||||5||Hippocrat||Do you know a mouseketeer?||||1||
Z||000000||Hippocrat||10-22-2001||03:46 AM||||M I C ,K E Y ,,,, M O U S E.. <P>You know who they are. That one person that "mickey mouses" everything. We were swapping an engine over the weekend. Well my friend who I will call mickey, does it every single time and it drives me insane. <P>First off some of the sensors had to be relocated and/or were of a different type. <BR>No problem right ? of course not because we can just cut this wire and forget about that sensor. When its all said and done? well we will just curse the car for being a piece of crap.<P>And heat shield ? we don't need no stinking heat shield, we'll just through that into the corner of the garage (they always make cars with extra parts anyway, right?)  <P>SO WHAT if the break pads don't fit.. we'll just file down these ones till they do. God forbid you leave em in the box and exchange them for the correct ones tomorrow.<P>You only truly need one nut on the motor mount any way. Really wheres it gonna go? <P>Emergency brakes are just a pain in the butt anyway why would you bother to hook them back up, when you can just zip tie them to the frame?<P>Oh the list goes on. And this guy has gotten better over the years.. <P>Don't get me wrong, this guy believe it or not, is brilliant (no really) just got his priorities messed up. <P>(Sorry for the long post) &lt;/RANT&gt;<P>But how many of you know/knew someone like this? Is it just me who goes absolutely insane over it? <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Hippocrat (edited 10-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||10-22-2001||12:23 PM||||I only know of 2- Christina Aguilera and Britney Spears.......and they can mess around my cars anytime they want. Ill even let them sing the mickey mouse club song as loud as they want   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 10-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Nashco||10-22-2001||01:17 PM||||Yeah, that kind of stuff drives me nuts!!!<P>I'm very very thorough and somewhat of a perfectionist.  For example, my dad harassed me for a while because I spent so much time rebuilding my VW engine (standard air cooled 1600).  Well, when I put it together, and after several thousand miles of hard abuse it still doesn't leak, that extra time pays off.  Oh, and if you've ever owned an air cooled VW, you know having no drops brand new is an accomplishment, let alone after a few days at 6k rpms in the sand dunes <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Usually the stuff that drives me nuts is when people wire stuff up, but route the wires poorly, or have bad connections.  Stereo installations seem to be the worst because you get some stereo-shop yahoo kid who thinks he's a pro, and wants to finish the job in 7 minutes.  Half the time you end up with cracked dash parts, stripped screws, shoddy connections, and a blown fuse or two because they cut a wrong wire and grounded something out.<P>Also drives me nuts when somebody is working with dirty parts and doesn't clean them up.  If you're re-installing something, there is ZERO reason not to get it like-new clean, and if you have access to an area that is hard or impossible to clean otherwise, why not clean it while you're in there?  Perhaps it isn't going to change anything, but it definitely isn't going to hurt anything.<P>Oh, the worst mickey mouse operation is not changing fluids.  They're cheap, and 99% of the time very easy to at least clean out the reservoir and refill it.  For fluid-dependent systems, this will at least double the life time; if you are too lazy to change the fluids it's only going to make you have to do some REAL work sooner than you want to.<P>There's my 2 cents...&lt;/bickering&gt;<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||9
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||10-22-2001||11:03 PM||||I AM NOT A PERFECTIONIST!!!<BR>Just because I grind off the casting flash on the inside AND outside of the block, as well as smooth the lettering and crap off till it is baby assed smooth...<BR>Oh wait, this is the MICKEY MOUSE CLUB...<BR>I don't work well with others...<BR>They don't live up to my standards...||||reg||1
